# Codex 0825-10, MED: no Content-Security-Policy existed anywhere (no
# _headers file, no <meta> tag). Cloudflare Pages reads this file format
# directly; GitHub Pages does not interpret it at all -- until Scott's DNS
# cutover (kids.simplyknown.co still serves from GitHub Pages as of this
# writing, see CLAUDE.md), this file ships but has NO live effect. Checked
# in now so the policy is ready and reviewed before that day, not another
# thing to remember on it.
#
# Real, not aspirational: this app has no build step and no nonce
# infrastructure, so every page's inline <script>/<style> stays allowed
# ('unsafe-inline') -- the actual XSS defense here is the textContent-not-
# innerHTML discipline proven in tests/hostile-input.test.mjs, not this
# header. What this DOES meaningfully add: no object/embed injection, no
# framing by another site (clickjacking), and every fetch/connect/frame
# target is an explicit, audited allow-list instead of "anything goes".
#
# The localStorage half of the original finding (sync key, Yoto tokens
# living in localStorage) is explicitly OUT of scope here -- that rides
# with Codex 0825-3 (single-device sync, ACCEPTED RISK, tracked separately
# as Stage 1b of the sync migration).
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; media-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://simplyknown-kids-sync.simplyknownfacts.workers.dev https://simplyknown-kids-sync-dev.simplyknownfacts.workers.dev https://api.yotoplay.com https://login.yotoplay.com; frame-src https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'
